  "steps": [
    "Preheat the oven to 375F and season the chicken generously with salt and pepper.",
    "Melt the butter in a large oven-safe skillet over medium heat. Add the chicken skin side down and cook until the skin is golden and releases easily, about 5 to 7 minutes.",
    "Flip and cook another 4 to 5 minutes, then transfer the skillet to the oven and roast until cooked through, about 15 minutes. Rest, then slice.",
    "Meanwhile, heat the sesame oil in a pot over medium. Add the ginger and garlic and cook until fragrant, about 1 minute.",
    "Add the soy sauce, mirin, stock and mushrooms. Simmer 15 to 20 minutes, then season with sea salt.",
    "Soft boil the eggs for 7 minutes, then shock in ice water and peel.",
    "Cook the ramen noodles separately according to the package, then drain.",
    "Divide the noodles between bowls, ladle over the broth, and top with sliced chicken, a halved egg, scallions and chili."
